        <mxCell id="qwhSnT7Znl6rGBa4y3Ik-81" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontFamily=Courier New;" value="This is how the drawings need to look&lt;div&gt;So we need to work left to right&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;So bassicALLY points come from the controller, throw terminal stip, but the terminal strip needs to be setup in a way that points may either use the terminal strip or not, if not the line should contiunue.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;the points will either be a field or MSSB point. but not both. so it should terminate as either of them is listed in the drawing.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;I think we should create the terminal strip like we did controllers, maybe a yml file in the project folder? that way we can also create a terminal strip drawing, so that if people are working are on the termainl strip they don&#39;t need to flick back and forth between all the drawings, as the controller drawing will not have all the info for the terminal strip&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="427" x="509" y="590" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
